      "fit": 0.65
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The border management agency, tasked with shaping the narrative of the U.S. border, recorded a numerical change—a spring weather-driven surge affecting an affected population of 8,268 individuals. This border activity metric, now in the hands of data interpreters, coexists with a powerful enforcement policy outcome: year-to-date immigration statistics remain low. The final act of this story, however, is stalled; an impasse among government officials has created a legislative stalemate over the funding bill, leaving the narrative's resolution in doubt.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Creator",
